@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Convert scheduled posts to manual publishing — CON-130.
# POST /api/posts/convert-to-manual moves posts from auto-publish
# (`scheduled`, a live Zernio job that WILL publish) to
# `scheduled_for_manual_publishing`, keeping scheduled_at. It's the
# server-side, disconnect-safe replacement for the old client-side
# cancel → poll → set-manual dance.
#
# Why it exists: turning OFF a platform's auto-publish allowlist entry
# does not touch posts already scheduled — their Zernio jobs still fire.
# This endpoint converts them in one call. Each post's Zernio job is
# cancelled by a background cancel_zernio_job task that then lands the
# post directly on scheduled_for_manual_publishing (no detour through
# ready_for_publish), so a post is never left unscheduled if the client
# disconnects mid-flight.
#
# All endpoints require authentication. Run "Login" from
# sessions/sessions.http first — the HTTP client stores and replays the
# cookie automatically.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - {{campaignId}} set (run campaigns/campaigns.http → createCampaign)
#
# Request shape — exactly one of:
#   { "platform": "linkedin" }       every scheduled post for the platform
#   { "post_ids": ["...", "..."] }   an explicit set
# `platform` is Zernio's wire id ("linkedin", "instagram", …), the same
# vocabulary the auto-publish allowlist uses — NOT the platform Sqid.
#
# Response — 202 with per-post outcomes:
#   { "converted": [id, …],                accepted (or already manual)
#     "failed":    [{ "id", "reason" }] }   not found / not convertible
# A post that publishes before its cancel lands is handled by the worker
# and recorded in the Post Log; it is not an error to swallow.

@linkedinPlatformId = AXqWG7U2qnpt
@futureAt = 2030-06-15T09:00:00Z

###
# ── Setup: stage two AUTO-scheduled LinkedIn posts ────────────────────────────
###

### Setup 1 — allowlist LinkedIn so scheduling routes to AUTO (scheduled)  [protected]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auto-publish-allowlist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platforms": ["linkedin"]
}

### Helper A — create a ready-to-publish LinkedIn post  [protected]
# @name convertReadyA
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
  "platform_id": "{{linkedinPlatformId}}",
  "platform_post_type": "article",
  "title": "Auto post A",
  "content": "Body A that already satisfies the publish rules.",
  "status": "ready_for_publish",
  "cta_type": "none"
}

> {% client.global.set("convertAId", response.body.id) %}

### Helper A — schedule it (allowlist ON → status becomes `scheduled`)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{convertAId}}/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scheduled_at": "{{futureAt}}"
}

### Helper B — create a second ready-to-publish LinkedIn post  [protected]
# @name convertReadyB
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
  "platform_id": "{{linkedinPlatformId}}",
  "platform_post_type": "article",
  "title": "Auto post B",
  "content": "Body B that already satisfies the publish rules.",
  "status": "ready_for_publish",
  "cta_type": "none"
}

> {% client.global.set("convertBId", response.body.id) %}

### Helper B — schedule it (allowlist ON → status becomes `scheduled`)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{convertBId}}/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scheduled_at": "{{futureAt}}"
}

### Setup 2 — turn OFF the LinkedIn allowlist (the real trigger)  [protected]
# From here on the setting reads "not allowed", but posts A and B are
# already `scheduled` and would still auto-publish — that's what the
# conversion below fixes.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auto-publish-allowlist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platforms": []
}

###
# ── Convert scenarios ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### 1. Convert EVERY scheduled post for a platform  [protected]
# Run Setup 1 + Helper A/B (create+schedule) first, then Setup 2.
# → 202 { converted: [A, B], failed: [] }  (each gets a cancel→manual job;
#   the posts stay `scheduled` until the worker lands them on
#   scheduled_for_manual_publishing — scheduled_at preserved).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "linkedin"
}

### 2. Convert an EXPLICIT set of posts  [protected]
# Same effect as (1) but for a hand-picked set rather than a whole platform.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "post_ids": ["{{convertAId}}", "{{convertBId}}"]
}

### 3. Mixed set — per-post outcomes  [protected]
# Create a plain DRAFT first (not schedulable → not convertible), then mix it
# with a scheduled post. → 202 { converted: [A], failed: [{ id: draft,
# reason: "post is not scheduled (status: draft)" }] }.
# @name convertDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
  "platform_id": "{{linkedinPlatformId}}",
  "platform_post_type": "article",
  "title": "Just a draft",
  "content": "Not scheduled.",
  "status": "draft",
  "cta_type": "none"
}

> {% client.global.set("convertDraftId", response.body.id) %}

### 3b. …now convert the scheduled post + the draft together  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "post_ids": ["{{convertAId}}", "{{convertDraftId}}"]
}

### 4. Unknown post id is reported as failed, not fatal  [protected]
# → 202 { converted: [], failed: [{ id: "nope", reason: "post not found" }] }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "post_ids": ["nope"]
}

### 5. Unsupported platform (expects 400)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "myspace"
}

### 6. Neither platform nor post_ids (expects 400)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 7. Both platform and post_ids (expects 400)  [protected]
# Exactly one selector must be set.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/convert-to-manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "linkedin",
  "post_ids": ["{{convertAId}}"]
}
